// =====================================================================
//  FluidXPro3: SYNTAX OVERVIEW (start here)
// =====================================================================
//
//  WHERE THIS FITS
//  ---------------
//  Developers write .fluid (plain English; see ../FLUID_SPEC.md).
//  `fluid build` turns it into .fx3, the strict layer described in this
//  folder. .fx3 can also be edited by hand. `fx3 build` then turns .fx3
//  into IR and then the target language (python or cpp, chosen by the
//  developer).
//
//  READING ORDER
//  -------------
//   1. lexical.fx3       comments, `;`, names, keywords, literals, annotation grammar
//   2. variables.fx3     simple variables: <type> <@annotations> <name> = <value>;
//   3. operators.fx3     arithmetic, comparison, logic, none-safety, precedence
//   4. types.fx3         inference, casts, maybe<T>, unpacking, aliases, generics
//   5. strings.fx3       text, f-strings, formatting, regex
//   6. collections.fx3   list, vector, array, set, map, tuple + method bank
//   7. structures.fx3    trees, graphs, heaps, filters, ... configured with annotations
//   8. constructs.fx3    function, looper + repeat, checker + switch, pipeline
//   9. enums.fx3         enums, enums with data, patterns
//  10. classes.fx3       classes, constructors, inheritance, interfaces
//  11. errors.fx3        @fails / try / catch / ?, panics, defer
//  12. memory.fx3        copy vs share, @ref / @move, borrowing, @unsafe
//  13. concurrency.fx3   async / await, spawn, locked / atomic, channels
//  14. modules.fx3       imports, packages, interop, fx3.toml
//  15. stdlib.fx3        the prelude and standard modules (outline)
//  16. compiler.fx3      build stages, the LLM's role, fx3.lock, diagnostics, CLI
//
//
//  THE LOCKED RULES (one place to check)
//  -------------------------------------
//  Shape
//   - Fixed shapes, flexible spellings. Built-in words match loosely
//     (case / _ / -); user names are exact and case-sensitive.
//   - Variable:    type @annotations name = value;
//   - Collection:  coll<inner @inner_annotations> @outer_annotations name = value;
//   - Construct:   kind[<inputs>|<outputs>] @annotations name = Kind(params) { }
//   - Brackets:    [ ] list-like   { } map / set   ( ) tuple
//   - `;` ends every statement. Blocks always use { }. Indentation has no meaning.
//
//  Values & types
//   - int is 64-bit. `/` always gives a float, `~/` gives an int (`//` is always a comment).
//     Overflow is an error.
//   - Automatic widening only. Narrowing needs `as` / `as?` / `as!`.
//   - Conditions must be bool. There is no truthiness.
//   - Only maybe<T> can be none, and it must be dealt with before use
//     (?? / if-bind / narrowing).
//   - "Not found" is always none, never -1.
//   - One unpacking syntax: type [a, b] = value;
//   - Ranges exclude the end (a..b). Use a..=b to include it.
//
//  Semantics
//   - Strings, collections and structures are COPIED (copy-on-write).
//     Class objects are SHARED (reference counted), unless the class is @value.
//   - No garbage collector. Memory is freed when the last owner goes away.
//   - Borrowing and data races are checked at compile time.
//     Raw pointers only inside @unsafe.
//   - Expected failures: @fails + must be handled. Bugs: panic, which
//     can't be caught.
//   - Methods are either ACTIONS (change things) or QUERIES (return
//     something new), never both.
//   - Classes: fields are private, methods are public, classes are final
//     unless @open, and @override is required.
//
//  LLM
//   - Used only on misses: unknown spellings, English outside the
//     mini-grammar, and Action bodies / values.
//   - Output is always canonical FluidX and is fully checked. Decisions
//     are recorded in fx3.lock, so builds are reproducible
//     (--offline / --no-llm).
//   - If it's unsure, the compiler asks. It never guesses silently.
//
//
//  NOT DESIGNED YET (next candidates)
//  ----------------------------------
//   - Standard library: scheduling, Process, async / await (the rest is in stdlib.fx3)
//   - Macros / compile-time code (comptime blocks, @comptime functions)
//   - Reflection (listing a class's fields at runtime, for Json and similar)
//   - Units of measure (5 km + 300 m)
//   - Interop details (Python runtime embedding, C ABI rules)
//   - Package registry and versioning rules
//   - Plugin system for user-defined annotations
